      en: "St. Philip's Parish Church is an Anglican church in St. Philip Parish, Barbados. The current building was constructed in 1836, replacing a 17th-century church. It is located inland and serves a rural congregation. The church is known for its simple Georgian design and a cemetery containing tombs of prominent planter families. The interior features a wooden vaulted ceiling and a historic organ. It remains an active parish church.",
